Scope of the above.

"This software" means everything in this repository that was written for it:
the React application, the build and verification scripts, the styling, and
the written content — the lessons under src/content/, the pages, and the rule,
glossary and unit text in src/lib/. No attribution is required for any of it.
Take it, print it, translate it, re-host it, sell it. It is sadaqah.

It does NOT cover the third-party material this repository redistributes,
whose own terms are not ours to relicense: the Qur'anic text in data/ and
src/content/quran.generated.json, the surah names, and the fonts. Those are
listed in NOTICE, and their terms travel with them wherever they go.

One request, which is a request and not a condition: this guide teaches
رواية حفص عن عاصم من طريق الشاطبيّة, and several points in it are disputed
among the scholars of the field and are written as disputed on purpose. If you
adapt it, please keep that nuance rather than flattening it. An oversimplified
ruling about the recitation of the Qur'an does real harm.
